Jahshaka patch 0088 - a voxelizer can be ASKED what it bound.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after pulling
this. It touches `Components/Hlms/Pbs/include/Vct/OgreVctVoxelizer.h`, which
patches 0061, 0062, 0064 and 0065 also touch; this one applies AFTER all four and
its single hunk sits below theirs. A tree that carries any of them and fails
`build-ogre.sh` with "upstream changed the patched file" is seeing the known
overlap false positive (CLAUDE.md): reset the ogre-next submodule and re-run the
whole stack.

THE MISSING READING. `VctVoxelizer` sizes every raster dispatch by
`QueuedInstance::numIndices`, filled in `placeItemsInBuckets` from
`getLodVao( subMesh, lodLevel )` - the LOD level patch 0064 keys the mesh entry by,
AND the clamp that patch applies to it. Nothing in the class reports that number.
A host that wants to know how much geometry a volume holds therefore has to walk
the mesh's VAOs from outside and re-implement the same clamp, which is a
PREDICTION: it agrees with the voxelizer only for as long as the two copies of the
clamp agree, and it counts geometry for an item the region declined. Jahshaka's
`GiStatus::CascadeStatus::voxelTriangles` was exactly that prediction (ATOM
inventory row AT-A12) and `gi.cascade_lod` asserted it against itself.

THE SHAPE. One const accessor, `getQueuedIndexCount()`, summing
`numIndices` over the buckets' queued instances. The buckets and not `mItems`,
because the buckets are what the dispatches iterate: an item the region declined
contributes nothing, which is the honest answer to "what does this volume hold".
Nothing is stored and nothing is computed at build time - the walk is over a few
hundred entries at most and a host reads it once per rebuild, beside
`getNumBuckets()` / `getNumOctants()` (patch 0065), which it is the missing third
of.

WHAT DOES NOT CHANGE. No behaviour: the class computes nothing new and no existing
member moves. Upstream's samples and every existing caller are untouched.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` on a tree carrying 0001-0087 and
`git apply --reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane
worktree. The suite is `gi.cascade_lod`, whose case 4 now asserts a READBACK of
what the voxelizer holds rather than the host's own prediction of it.

--- a/Components/Hlms/Pbs/include/Vct/OgreVctVoxelizer.h
+++ b/Components/Hlms/Pbs/include/Vct/OgreVctVoxelizer.h
@@ -438,6 +438,39 @@
         /// report it (Jahshaka: GiStatus::CascadeStatus::voxelDispatches).
         size_t getNumBuckets() const { return mBuckets.size(); }
         size_t getNumOctants() const { return mOctants.size(); }
+
+        /// JAHSHAKA PATCH 0088 - HOW MANY INDICES THE LAST build() ACTUALLY BOUND.
+        ///
+        /// `QueuedInstance::numIndices` is what sizes each raster dispatch, and it
+        /// is filled in `placeItemsInBuckets` from `getLodVao( subMesh, lodLevel )`
+        /// (patch 0064) - i.e. from the LOD LEVEL this voxelizer resolved and
+        /// CLAMPED for itself. Summing it is therefore a READING of the geometry
+        /// the volume holds, where a host walking the mesh's VAOs from outside can
+        /// only ever produce a prediction that re-implements the clamp and drifts
+        /// from it (Jahshaka: GiStatus::CascadeStatus::voxelTriangles used to be
+        /// exactly that prediction).
+        ///
+        /// Counted over the buckets and not over `mItems`, because the buckets are
+        /// what the dispatches iterate: an item the region declined contributes
+        /// nothing here, which is the honest answer.
+        size_t getQueuedIndexCount() const
+        {
+            size_t total = 0u;
+            VoxelizerBucketMap::const_iterator itor = mBuckets.begin();
+            VoxelizerBucketMap::const_iterator endt = mBuckets.end();
+            while( itor != endt )
+            {
+                FastArray<QueuedInstance>::const_iterator itInst = itor->second.queuedInst.begin();
+                FastArray<QueuedInstance>::const_iterator enInst = itor->second.queuedInst.end();
+                while( itInst != enInst )
+                {
+                    total += itInst->numIndices;
+                    ++itInst;
+                }
+                ++itor;
+            }
+            return total;
+        }
     public:
